---
import { ButtonLink, Callout, Icon, Link } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'

import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro'
import { SITE } from '../../site.config'
---

<Docs title="Install" description="Install Dep Beacon for VS Code or Zed.">
  <header class="docs-page-header">
    <p class="docs-eyebrow"><span>01</span> / Getting started</p>
    <h1>Install once.<br />Open your manifest.</h1>
    <p class="docs-intro">Add Dep Beacon to VS Code or Zed. Dependency signals appear where you already work.</p>
    <dl class="docs-facts">
      <div><dt>Setup</dt><dd>No configuration required</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Supported files</dt><dd>JSON, JSONC + YAML manifests</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="install-vscode">
    <h2 id="install-vscode">In VS Code</h2>
    <ol class="docs-steps" role="list">
      <li><strong>Find the extension.</strong><p>Open the Extensions view and search for <code>Dep
        Beacon</code>.</p></li>
      <li><strong>Select Install.</strong><p>Choose the extension published by <code>santi020k</code>.</p></li>
      <li><strong>Open a manifest.</strong><p>Use <code>package.json</code>, <code>pnpm-workspace.yaml</code>, or
        <code>pnpm-workspace.yml</code>.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="docs-actions">
      <ButtonLink class="docs-primary-action" href={SITE.marketplaceUrl} newTab variant="unstyled">
        Get it from Marketplace <span><Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></span>
      </ButtonLink>
      <ButtonLink class="docs-text-action" href={SITE.openVsxUrl} newTab variant="unstyled">
        Open VSX <Icon name="arrow-up-right" />
      </ButtonLink>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="install-zed">
    <h2 id="install-zed">In Zed</h2>
    <ol class="docs-steps" role="list">
      <li><strong>Open extensions.</strong><p>Open the command palette and run <code>zed: extensions</code>.</p></li>
      <li><strong>Install Dep Beacon.</strong><p>Search for <code>Dep Beacon</code> and select Install. Use version
        <code>0.0.3</code> or newer for the workflow described here.</p></li>
      <li><strong>Open a manifest.</strong><p>The same package and pnpm workspace files are supported. No settings
        are required.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <Callout class="docs-note">
      <strong>Already have the file open?</strong>
      <p>Focus the manifest and run <code>editor: restart language server</code> once after installation or an
        extension update. Reopening the manifest works too.</p>
    </Callout>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="first-signals">
    <h2 id="first-signals">Your first signals</h2>
    <p>
      Dep Beacon activates automatically for supported manifests. Both editors show dependency diagnostics and update
      actions. VS Code also provides inline decorations; Zed uses its native diagnostics multi-buffer and
        code-action menu.
    </p>
    <p>
      In VS Code, <code>depBeacon.showInlineStatus</code> controls inline labels,
      <code>depBeacon.checkVulnerabilities</code> controls OSV queries, and <code>depBeacon.packageManager</code>
      overrides automatic package-manager detection. See <Link href="/docs/configuration">configuration</Link> for
        the defaults.
    </p>
  </section>

  <nav class="docs-next" aria-label="Choose your editor guide">
    <Link href="/docs/vscode-extension">Explore VS Code <Icon name="arrow-right" /></Link>
    <Link href="/docs/zed-extension">Explore Zed <Icon name="arrow-right" /></Link>
  </nav>
</Docs>
